    "dex.bloomara": "The full bloom of its wings plays four bars no composer has transcribed without weeping. It molts once a year; collectors fight over the husks.",
    "dex.brookoda": "It ends every swim with the same three settling notes - its coda - before sliding under the bank. Anglers pack up when they hear it; the fish already have.",
    "dex.galliard": "It dances its namesake five-step on thermals, kicking off each measure with a wingtip snap. Festival crowds clap along; the Galliard never misses the beat - they do.",
    "dex.hummble": "Its wingbeat sits exactly on the region's root note, and hives of them keep Cantorel's meadows in tune. Beekeepers here are called choirmasters.",
    "dex.lichenore": "Centuries of moss have mineralized into a singing crust along its back. It moves twice a day, and the forest schedules around it.",
    "dex.mossoon": "It naps under a quilt of moss it hums to itself, one bar at a time. Whole logs go green where a Mossoon family winters.",
    "dex.petalune": "Its wing-petals shed a chiming pollen that hangs in moonlight. Arbor Vale brides time their processions to the petalune drift.",
    "dex.shrubato": "It trims hedges flat with its incisors, always to the same tempo. Untended gardens in Arbor Vale stay suspiciously well-kept.",
    "dex.thornata": "Its bramble pelt tightens a half-step when threatened, sounding a chord most predators have learned by heart. Conservatory gardeners prune around a Thornata, never near one.",
    "dex.torrentet": "Four voices share its throat, and white water is simply their rehearsal space. Bridge pilings near a Torrentet den wear away in chord patterns.",
    "motif.bloomara": "Bloomara",
    "motif.brookoda": "Brookoda",
